The DirectoryBrowser work from last turn was committed (as a prior iteration); only this turn's `StringUtils` change remains in the working tree. The diff is clean.

## This turn's refactoring: `StringUtils.concat` deduplication

The two `concat` overloads — `concat(String separator, Class<?>...)` and `concat(String separator, String...)` — had byte-for-byte identical separator-joining loops, differing only in that the first converts each element via `classname(...)`. I removed the duplicated loop by having the `Class<?>...` overload map each type to its name and delegate to the `String...` overload:

```java
public static String concat(String separator, Class<?>... types) {
    if (types == null || types.length == 0) {
        return Constants.EMPTY_STRING;
    }

    String[] names = new String[types.length];
    for (int i = 0; i < types.length; i++) {
        names[i] = classname(types[i]);
    }

    return concat(separator, names);
}
```

The `null`/empty guard is retained (delegating a `null` array would NPE on `.length`), and `classname(null)` NPEs identically whether called inline or during the pre-mapping, so the change is behavior-preserving. Single-file, no API change.

## Verification
- `TypeRenderUtilsTest` (exercises `concat` through all 8 call sites) — **11/11 pass**.
- `StringUtilsTest` — **48/48 pass**.
- `git diff --check` — clean.

